	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000211','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','There are 1,000 bottles, exactly one poisoned, and one simultaneous test round. Each strip reports whether any tested drop was poisoned. What is the fewest strips needed to identify the bottle?','["100","10","9","11"]','"10"','Assign each bottle a unique 10-bit label and put a drop on the strips for its 1 bits. Ten strips distinguish 2^10=1,024 outcomes.','Original binary encoding puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000212','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Exactly one of 128 bottles is poisoned. With one test round and one bit per test strip, what is the minimum number of strips?','["8","128","7","6"]','"7"','Seven binary results distinguish 2^7=128 bottles, so seven strips suffice and fewer cannot encode all bottles.','Original binary encoding puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000213','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A row of 20 prisoners each wears a black or white hat. Each sees only hats ahead; from the back forward each says one color, hearing earlier answers. They agree that the first answer states the parity of black hats ahead. How many prisoners can they guarantee save?','["20","10","0","19"]','"19"','The first prisoner may be wrong because that answer encodes parity. Each later prisoner uses the announced parity and prior answers to infer their own hat, guaranteeing the other 19.','Original parity puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000214','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Three coins are labeled A, B and C. One is counterfeit and is known to be heavier. What is the fewest balance-scale weighings needed to identify it?','["1","2","3","0"]','"1"','Weigh A against B: if they balance, C is heavy; otherwise the heavier pan identifies the counterfeit.','Original weighing puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000215','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','There are three switches outside a closed room and one ordinary incandescent bulb inside. You may enter the room once. What can identify the switch?','["Impossible even with heat","Turn one on for a while, turn it off, turn a second on; use light and bulb warmth","Flip all three quickly","Only listen at the door"]','"Turn one on for a while, turn it off, turn a second on; use light and bulb warmth"','A lit bulb maps to the second switch; a warm unlit bulb to the first; a cold unlit bulb to the third.','Original switch puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000216','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two doors lead to safety and danger. One guard always lies and one always tells truth; you do not know which guard is which. What should you ask either guard?','["Ask both guards separately and choose the first answer","Ask which door is dangerous and take that one","Which door would the other guard say is safe? Then take the opposite door","Are you the truthful guard? Then take the door they point to"]','"Which door would the other guard say is safe? Then take the opposite door"','Either guard points to the unsafe door when asked what the other would identify as safe, so choose the other door.','Original truth-teller puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000217','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two ropes each take exactly 60 minutes to burn, but burn at nonuniform rates. How can you measure exactly 45 minutes?','["Light both ropes at one end and wait until either ends","Cut one rope in half and burn one half","Light one rope at both ends only","Light rope 1 at both ends and rope 2 at one end; when rope 1 ends, light the other end of rope 2"]','"Light rope 1 at both ends and rope 2 at one end; when rope 1 ends, light the other end of rope 2"','Rope 1 finishes in 30 minutes. Rope 2 then has 30 minutes of burn-time left; lighting its other end makes it finish in 15 more, totaling 45.','Original rope puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000218','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Three boxes are labeled Apples, Oranges and Mixed, and every label is wrong. You may draw one fruit from one box. From which box should you draw?','["The box labeled Mixed","The box labeled Apples","The box labeled Oranges","Any box works equally well"]','"The box labeled Mixed"','Because the Mixed label is wrong, that box contains only one fruit type. Its draw identifies that type; the two remaining incorrect labels then determine the other boxes.','Original mislabeled-box puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000219','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Four people need to cross a bridge at night with one torch. Their crossing times are 1, 2, 7 and 10 minutes; at most two cross together and a pair moves at the slower speed. What is the minimum total time?','["21 minutes","17 minutes","19 minutes","20 minutes"]','"17 minutes"','Send 1&2 (2), 1 back (1), 7&10 (10), 2 back (2), 1&2 (2): total 17 minutes.','Original bridge puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000220','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A farmer must ferry a fox, a chicken and grain across a river. The boat carries the farmer and one item. The fox cannot be left with the chicken, and the chicken cannot be left with grain. What must the farmer take across first?','["The grain","Any one is safe","The chicken","The fox"]','"The chicken"','Taking the chicken first prevents either forbidden pair from being left alone; the farmer can then shuttle the fox and grain safely.','Original river-crossing puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000221','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','There are 100 prisoners, one designated counter, and a light switch initially off. Assume every prisoner enters the room infinitely many times, the counter can recognize each visitor, and everyone knows this schedule. Every non-counter may turn the switch on once, only when it is off; they never turn it off. The counter turns it off and adds one whenever finding it on. What count lets the counter know all 99 others have visited?','["101","99","50","100"]','"99"','Each of the 99 non-counters can signal exactly once by changing the switch from off to on. The counter records one for each such signal and turns it off; because visits repeat forever, all 99 signals will eventually be observed.','Original coordination puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000222','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A number is between 1 and 100 inclusive. You may ask yes/no questions and are told whether it is higher or lower after each guess. What is the maximum number of guesses needed with optimal strategy?','["7","6","8","50"]','"7"','Binary search over 100 possibilities needs ceil(log2(100))=7 yes/no comparisons in the worst case.','Original binary-search puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000223','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You have 9 identical-looking balls; one is heavier. What is the fewest balance-scale weighings needed to find it?','["4","2","1","3"]','"2"','Weigh 3 against 3. If balanced, the heavy ball is among the remaining 3; otherwise it is in the heavier group. A second 1-versus-1 identifies it or leaves the third.','Original weighing puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000224','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A clock takes 5 seconds to strike 6 times, with equal intervals between strikes. How long does it take to strike 12 times?','["12 seconds","6 seconds","11 seconds","10 seconds"]','"11 seconds"','Six strikes have five intervals, so each interval is 1 second. Twelve strikes have eleven intervals and take 11 seconds.','Original interval puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000225','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A code has three distinct digits from 1–5. How many possible codes are there if order matters?','["15","125","10","60"]','"60"','There are 5 choices for the first digit, 4 for the second and 3 for the third: 5×4×3=60.','Original counting puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000226','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You have two identical-looking eggs and a 100-floor building. An egg breaks if dropped above an unknown threshold floor and survives at or below it. In the worst case, what is the fewest drops needed to guarantee finding the threshold?','["14","10","13","20"]','"14"','With 14 drops, test floors 14, 27, 39, 50 and so on, reducing the step by one each time; 14+13+…+1=105 covers 100 floors. Thirteen drops cover only 91.','Original egg-dropping puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000227','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','In a room of 23 people, what is the approximate probability that at least two share a birthday, assuming 365 equally likely birthdays and ignoring leap days?','["About 90%","About 50%","About 10%","About 25%"]','"About 50%"','The exact probability of a shared birthday is 1−(365×364×…×343)/365^23, about 50.7%.','Original birthday puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000228','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A man looks at a portrait and says, “Brothers and sisters I have none, but that man’s father is my father’s son.” Who is in the portrait?','["His uncle","Himself","His son","His father"]','"His son"','Since he has no siblings, “my father’s son” means himself; the portrait’s father is him, so the pictured man is his son.','Original deduction puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000229','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A farmer has 17 sheep; all but 9 run away. How many remain?','["8","17","0","9"]','"9"','“All but 9” means nine did not run away.','Original wording-and-logic puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000230','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Five machines make five widgets in five minutes at a constant rate. How long do 100 machines take to make 100 widgets?','["5 minutes","100 minutes","20 minutes","1 minute"]','"5 minutes"','Each machine makes one widget in five minutes; 100 machines work in parallel and make 100 widgets in five minutes.','Original rate puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000231','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A lily pad patch doubles in area each day. If it covers the whole pond on day 48, on what day was half the pond covered?','["Day 1","Day 47","Day 24","Day 46"]','"Day 47"','Doubling from half to full takes one day, so half coverage occurred on day 47.','Original backward-reasoning puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000232','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Eight identical-looking balls include one ball heavier than the other seven. Using a balance scale and at most two weighings, which strategy guarantees finding the heavier ball?','["Weigh 2 vs 2 twice","Weigh 7 vs 1, then compare any two","Weigh 3 vs 3; if balanced weigh the last 2 against each other, otherwise weigh 1 vs 1 from the heavier group","Weigh 4 vs 4, then weigh the heavier side"]','"Weigh 3 vs 3; if balanced weigh the last 2 against each other, otherwise weigh 1 vs 1 from the heavier group"','First weigh three balls against three. If they balance, the heavier ball is among the two set aside, so one weighing identifies it. If they do not balance, it is in the heavier group of three; weigh two of those against each other. If they balance, the third is heavier; otherwise the heavier side identifies it.','Original weighing puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000233','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Four cards show A, D, 4 and 7. Each has a letter on one side and a number on the other. To test “if a card has a vowel, its reverse is even,” which cards must you turn over?','["A and 4","D and 7","All four","A and 7"]','"A and 7"','Turn A to check its reverse is even. Turn 7 because a vowel on its reverse would disprove the rule. D and 4 cannot falsify the conditional.','Original conditional-reasoning puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000234','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A sealed room has one candle, one match, a lamp and a fireplace. What do you light first?','["The match","The candle","The lamp","The fireplace"]','"The match"','You need to light the match first before using it to light any other object.','Original attention puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000235','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A prisoner sees 99 hats ahead. Each hat is either red or blue. The last prisoner’s answer is allowed to be wrong, but all can hear it. What single fact can that first answer encode so the other 99 can determine their own hats?','["A random guess","Parity of the number of red hats ahead","The exact full sequence of hats","The last prisoner’s own hat color"]','"Parity of the number of red hats ahead"','One bit has two states and can encode even/odd parity; each later prisoner combines it with seen and heard colors to infer their own.','Original parity puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','logic',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000236','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person walks into a room, sees a table with 10 candles, and blows out 3. The room has no drafts and the other candles stay lit. How many candles are still burning?','["10","0","7","3"]','"7"','Seven were not blown out and remain lit; the three blown-out candles are not burning.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000237','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A cold glass is taken from a refrigerator into warm humid air. After a few minutes, droplets appear on the outside. Where did the water come from?','["Water leaked through the glass","The glass produced water","Water came from inside the glass","Water vapor in the air condensed on the cold glass"]','"Water vapor in the air condensed on the cold glass"','Humid air touching the cold surface cools below its dew point, so water vapor condenses on the outside.','Original everyday-science lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000238','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A sealed bottle is full of water. You put it in a freezer until the water becomes ice. What happens to the water’s volume?','["It expands","It shrinks","It stays exactly the same","It disappears"]','"It expands"','Water expands as it freezes, which is why a full sealed bottle can crack.','Original everyday-science lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000239','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A driver goes the wrong way down a one-way street, passes a police officer, and is not stopped. The driver is walking, not driving. Why?','["The walker is invisible","The one-way restriction applies to vehicles, and the person is walking","The officer is asleep","The street has no direction"]','"The one-way restriction applies to vehicles, and the person is walking"','A pedestrian walking down the street is not driving a vehicle against the one-way traffic rule.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000240','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person pushes a small car to a hotel and immediately knows they are bankrupt. What kind of car is this?','["A toy remote-control car","A rental car","A token in a board game","A real automobile"]','"A token in a board game"','The person is playing Monopoly; moving the token to a hotel property can require a payment they cannot afford.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000241','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A skydiver is found in an open field after jumping from an aircraft. The unopened pack strapped to their back is intact. What most likely happened?','["They forgot their lunch","The pack contained books","The field moved under them","The parachute in the pack failed to open"]','"The parachute in the pack failed to open"','The pack is specified as the skydiver’s parachute pack; an unopened parachute explains the fatal fall.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000242','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A man shaves many people every day, yet he has a beard. What is his job?','["Barber","Surgeon","Actor","Chef"]','"Barber"','The barber shaves other people, not necessarily himself.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000243','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person reads a printed page in a room with no electric lights. The room has an uncovered window. What is the simplest light source?','["The ink","Daylight","The paper itself","A hidden flashlight"]','"Daylight"','The uncovered window allows daylight into the room, making the page visible without electric lighting.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000244','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A dog walks across the solid frozen surface of a river without getting wet. It does not fly, swim, or use a bridge, boat, or tunnel. What makes the crossing possible?','["The river has dried up","The dog is carried by a bird","The river’s surface is frozen","The dog is invisible"]','"The river’s surface is frozen"','The dog stays dry because it walks on the frozen surface; the stated conditions rule out other crossing methods.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000245','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Using standard U.S. coins, a person has two coins totaling 30 cents. One of the coins is not a dime. Which pair can they have?','["Two dimes","A half-dollar and a dime","Three nickels","A quarter and a nickel"]','"A quarter and a nickel"','A quarter plus a nickel totals 30 cents, and neither coin is a dime; therefore the statement that one is not a dime is true.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000246','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A train is electric and travels north. The wind blows south. Which way does its smoke blow?','["It produces no exhaust smoke","North","South","East"]','"It produces no exhaust smoke"','An electric train does not produce combustion exhaust smoke.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000247','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person has 12 eggs. They break 2, fry 2 and eat 2. If the same 2 eggs are used for all three actions, how many eggs remain whole and unused?','["4","10","6","8"]','"10"','The same two eggs are broken, fried and eaten, so 12−2=10 remain whole and unused.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000248','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person is standing in a room with a clock that reads 3:15. What is the smaller angle between the clock hands?','["15 degrees","22.5 degrees","7.5 degrees","0 degrees"]','"7.5 degrees"','At 3:15 the minute hand is at 90°. The hour hand has moved 7.5° past 3, to 97.5°, so the difference is 7.5°.','Original lateral math puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000249','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person throws a ball as hard as possible. It returns to them without hitting anything, and no one else touches it. How?','["They throw it into a mirror","A magnet pulls it back","It is attached to a string","They throw it straight upward"]','"They throw it straight upward"','Gravity brings a vertically thrown ball back to the thrower, assuming negligible horizontal motion and no obstruction.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000250','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A letter travels around the world while its postage stamp stays in one corner. Which corner is meant?','["A corner of the envelope","A corner of the map","A room corner","A street corner"]','"A corner of the envelope"','The stamp is attached to a corner of the envelope, and the letter carries it around the world.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000251','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A child falls off a 20-meter ladder onto concrete but is unhurt. The child fell from the lowest rung while standing on the ground. Why?','["The fall happened underwater","The child was on the bottom rung, at ground level","The ladder was made of foam","The child landed on a trampoline"]','"The child was on the bottom rung, at ground level"','The lowest rung is at ground level, so the fall height is essentially zero.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000252','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A 3-meter ladder leans against a wall. Its foot slides 1 meter farther from the wall while the top remains against the wall. What happens to the height of the top?','["It stays at the same height","It becomes 1 meter high","It moves down","It moves up"]','"It moves down"','The ladder length stays fixed. Increasing the horizontal leg of the right triangle requires the vertical leg to decrease.','Original geometry lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000253','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person must cross a 10-meter room without walking, running, jumping or being carried. The room is empty and level. What is a valid solution?','["Fly across","Use a hidden tunnel","Ask someone to carry them","Slide across the floor"]','"Slide across the floor"','Sliding is movement across the room but is none of the prohibited methods.','Original lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000254','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person sees a house with all four walls facing south. A bear walks past it. What color is the bear?','["White","Brown","Black","The information is insufficient"]','"White"','A house whose walls all face south can be at the North Pole; a bear there is a polar bear, which is white.','Original geography lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000255','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person is born on December 31 and celebrates their birthday two days later. What date is it?','["December 31","January 2","January 1","December 30"]','"January 2"','Two days after December 31 is January 2.','Original calendar lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000256','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A man says he was born in 1990 and died in 1980, yet he was 30 years old. How is that possible?','["He was a time traveler","It is impossible","1990 and 1980 are room numbers, not years","He traveled backward in time"]','"1990 and 1980 are room numbers, not years"','The numbers can be labels such as hospital room numbers; the statement does not say they are years.','Original ambiguity-check puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000257','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A store gives a 20% discount and then adds 20% tax to the discounted price. Starting from $100, what is the final price?','["$100","$104","$80","$96"]','"$96"','The discount gives $80; 20% tax on $80 is $16, so the final price is $96. Percent changes apply to different bases.','Original percentage lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000258','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A person says, “The day before yesterday I was 25; this year I turn 27, and next year I will be 28.” Assuming one birthday each year, what date could today be?','["January 1, with birthday on December 31","June 1, with birthday on May 31","December 30, with birthday on December 29","The dates cannot work"]','"January 1, with birthday on December 31"','On January 1, the person was 25 on December 30, turned 26 on December 31, and will turn 27 on December 31 later this year; on the next December 31 they will turn 28.','Original calendar lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000259','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A shop sells a hat for $10; the hat cost the shop $10. A customer pays with a counterfeit $20 bill and receives $10 change. What is the shop’s loss?','["$0","$20","$10","$30"]','"$20"','The shop loses the $10 change and the $10-cost hat, totaling $20. The counterfeit bill has no value.','Original accounting lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000260','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A room contains 5 people. Each person shakes hands with every other person exactly once. How many handshakes occur?','["5","25","10","20"]','"10"','Each handshake is an unordered pair, so there are 5×4/2=10 pairs.','Original counting lateral puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','lateral',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000261','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair coin is flipped twice. What is the probability of getting heads both times?','["1/2","1/3","3/4","1/4"]','"1/4"','The independent flips each have probability 1/2 of heads, so both heads has probability 1/2×1/2=1/4.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000262','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Roll one fair six-sided die. What is the probability of rolling an even number?','["1/2","1/3","2/3","1/6"]','"1/2"','Three of the six equally likely faces are even: 2, 4 and 6.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000263','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Roll two fair six-sided dice. What is the probability that their sum is 7?','["1/4","1/6","1/12","1/9"]','"1/6"','Six of the 36 equally likely ordered outcomes sum to 7, so the probability is 6/36=1/6.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000264','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Draw one card from a standard 52-card deck. What is the probability it is an ace?','["1/52","4/13","1/13","1/4"]','"1/13"','There are four aces among 52 cards, so 4/52=1/13.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000265','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Draw two cards without replacement from a standard 52-card deck. What is the probability both are aces?','["1/169","1/26","1/52","1/221"]','"1/221"','The probability is 4/52×3/51=12/2652=1/221.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000266','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair coin is flipped three times. What is the probability of exactly two heads?','["3/8","1/4","1/2","5/8"]','"3/8"','There are three outcomes with exactly two heads (HHT, HTH, THH) among eight equally likely sequences.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000267','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A bag has 3 red and 2 blue balls. Draw two without replacement. What is the probability of red then blue?','["1/2","3/10","1/5","2/5"]','"3/10"','The probability is 3/5×2/4=6/20=3/10.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000268','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair coin is flipped twice. What is the probability of getting at least one head?','["1/4","1","3/4","1/2"]','"3/4"','The only outcome with no heads is TT, with probability 1/4; the complement is 3/4.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000269','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair eight-section spinner is numbered 1 through 8. What is the probability of landing on a multiple of 3?','["3/8","1/3","1/8","1/4"]','"1/4"','Only 3 and 6 qualify, so 2 of 8 outcomes gives probability 1/4.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000270','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Choose one integer uniformly from 1 through 10. What is the probability it is divisible by 2 or 3?','["7/10","6/10","5/10","8/10"]','"7/10"','The qualifying values are 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9 and 10: seven of ten values.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000271','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair four-sided die is numbered 1 through 4. What is the probability of rolling a number greater than 2?','["1/3","1/2","1/4","3/4"]','"1/2"','Two of the four faces, 3 and 4, are greater than 2.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000272','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two fair dice are rolled. What is the probability that at least one shows a 6?','["1/3","1/2","11/36","1/6"]','"11/36"','Use the complement: neither die is 6 with probability 25/36, so at least one six is 11/36.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000273','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A box contains 4 green and 6 yellow balls. Draw two without replacement. What is the probability both are green?','["4/25","1/5","1/3","2/15"]','"2/15"','The probability is 4/10×3/9=12/90=2/15.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000274','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair coin is flipped twice. Given that at least one flip is heads, what is the probability both flips are heads?','["1/3","1/2","1/4","2/3"]','"1/3"','Conditioning on at least one head leaves HH, HT and TH equally likely; one of these three is HH.','Original conditional-probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000275','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair coin is flipped four times. What is the probability of four heads?','["1/32","1/16","1/8","1/4"]','"1/16"','Four independent heads each have probability 1/2, so the result is (1/2)^4=1/16.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000276','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Choose two distinct numbers uniformly from 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. What is the probability their sum is even?','["3/5","1/5","2/5","1/2"]','"2/5"','The sum is even when both numbers are odd or both even: C(3,2)+C(2,2)=4 favorable pairs out of C(5,2)=10, so 2/5.','Original combinatorics puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000277','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A bag has 3 red and 2 blue balls. Draw one, replace it, then draw again. What is the probability both draws are the same color?','["9/25","2/5","1/2","13/25"]','"13/25"','Same color means RR or BB: (3/5)^2+(2/5)^2=9/25+4/25=13/25.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000278','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A drawer has 4 black socks and 3 white socks. In the dark, how many socks must you take to guarantee a matching-color pair?','["3","2","4","7"]','"3"','With two colors, the worst first two picks are one of each; the third must match one of them.','Original pigeonhole puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000279','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','One card is drawn from a standard 52-card deck. What is the probability it is a heart or a king?','["1/2","4/13","17/52","1/4"]','"4/13"','There are 13 hearts plus 4 kings, with the king of hearts counted twice, giving 16 distinct cards; 16/52=4/13.','Original inclusion-exclusion puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000280','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair six-sided die is rolled twice. What is the probability of getting a 1 on both rolls?','["1/6","1/18","1/36","1/12"]','"1/36"','The rolls are independent, so 1/6×1/6=1/36.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000281','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Choose one integer uniformly from 1 through 10. What is the probability it is prime?','["1/2","3/10","1/5","2/5"]','"2/5"','The primes are 2, 3, 5 and 7, so 4 of 10 choices are prime: 2/5.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000282','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','In a fair coin flip, what is the probability the result is tails?','["1/2","1/4","1/3","1"]','"1/2"','A fair coin has two equally likely outcomes, and one is tails.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000283','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair six-sided die is rolled once. What is the probability of a result less than 3?','["2/3","1/3","1/2","1/6"]','"1/3"','The qualifying faces are 1 and 2, so 2/6=1/3.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000284','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A fair coin is flipped three times. What is the probability of no heads?','["1/2","3/8","1/8","1/4"]','"1/8"','No heads means TTT, one sequence among 2^3=8 equally likely sequences.','Original probability puzzle; calculation in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000285','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A single-elimination tournament begins with 8 teams and has no byes. How many games are required to produce one champion?','["8","4","15","7"]','"7"','Each game eliminates one team; reducing 8 teams to 1 requires 7 eliminations and therefore 7 games.','Original tournament probability/counting puzzle; proof in explanation','https://github.com/pattarapolj/carpool-gaming/blob/main/docs/delivery/question-bank-review.md','probability',180),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000286','ESTIMATE','About how many kilometers is Earth’s equatorial circumference? Round to the nearest whole kilometer.',NULL,'40075','Earth’s equatorial circumference is about 40,075 km.','NASA: Earth Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/earth/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000287','ESTIMATE','About how many kilometers wide is the Sun? Round to the nearest ten thousand kilometers.',NULL,'1390000','The Sun’s diameter is about 1,392,700 km, which rounds to 1,390,000 km.','NASA: Sun Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/sun/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000288','ESTIMATE','About how many kilometers separate Earth and the Moon on average? Round to the nearest thousand kilometers.',NULL,'384000','The average Earth–Moon distance is approximately 384,400 km, rounding to 384,000 km at the nearest thousand.','NASA: Moon Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/moon/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000289','ESTIMATE','About how many kilometers per second does light travel in vacuum? Round to the nearest thousand.',NULL,'300000','The defined speed of light is 299,792.458 km/s, which rounds to 300,000 km/s.','NIST: Speed of light','https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?c','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000290','ESTIMATE','About how many Earth years does Jupiter take to orbit the Sun? Round to the nearest whole year.',NULL,'12','Jupiter completes an orbit in about 11.86 Earth years, which rounds to 12.','NASA: Jupiter Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/jupiter/jupiter-facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000291','ESTIMATE','About how many hours long is one Martian day? Round to the nearest whole hour.',NULL,'25','A Mars solar day is about 24 hours and 39 minutes, which rounds to 25 hours.','NASA: Mars Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/mars/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000292','ESTIMATE','At standard sea-level pressure, about how many degrees Celsius does pure water boil at? Enter the whole number.',NULL,'100','At standard atmospheric pressure, water boils at 100°C.','NIST Chemistry WebBook: Water','https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C7732185','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000293','ESTIMATE','About how many meters high is Mount Everest above sea level? Round to the nearest meter.',NULL,'8849','Nepal and China report the recognized height as 8,848.86 m, rounding to 8,849 m.','Survey Department of Nepal: Mount Everest height','https://dos.gov.np/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000294','ESTIMATE','About how many meters tall is the Eiffel Tower including its current antenna? Enter the whole number.',NULL,'330','The Eiffel Tower is 330 m high including its antenna.','Eiffel Tower Official Site: Key figures','https://www.toureiffel.paris/en/the-monument/key-figures','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000295','ESTIMATE','About how many meters tall is the Statue of Liberty from ground to torch tip, including its pedestal? Enter the whole number.',NULL,'93','The National Park Service gives the full height from ground to torch as 305 feet, about 93 m.','U.S. National Park Service: Statue of Liberty','https://www.nps.gov/stli/learn/historyculture/statue-statistics.htm','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000296','ESTIMATE','About how many meters long is the Golden Gate Bridge’s main span? Round to the nearest ten meters.',NULL,'1280','The main span is 4,200 feet, or about 1,280 m.','Golden Gate Bridge Highway and Transportation District: Facts','https://www.goldengate.org/bridge/history-research/statistics-data/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000297','ESTIMATE','About how many degrees is Earth’s axial tilt relative to its orbital plane? Round to one decimal place and enter the number without a degree sign.',NULL,'23.4','Earth’s axial tilt is about 23.4 degrees, which drives the seasons.','NASA Space Place: What causes the seasons?','https://spaceplace.nasa.gov/seasons/en/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000298','ESTIMATE','About how many bones are in a typical adult human skeleton? Enter the commonly cited count.',NULL,'206','A typical adult human skeleton has 206 bones; individual variation exists as some bones fuse.','Cleveland Clinic: How many bones are in the human body?','https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/21753-bones','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000299','ESTIMATE','About what percentage of an adult human body by mass is water? Round to the nearest ten percent.',NULL,'60','Water makes up roughly 60 percent of adult body mass, with variation between people.','U.S. Geological Survey: The Water in You','https://www.usgs.gov/special-topics/water-science-school/science/water-you-water-and-human-body','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000300','ESTIMATE','About how many million kilometers is Earth from the Sun on average? Round to the nearest million.',NULL,'150','One astronomical unit, the mean Earth–Sun distance, is approximately 149.6 million km, rounding to 150 million.','NASA: Solar System Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/solar-system-facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000301','ESTIMATE','About how many days does Earth take to orbit the Sun? Round to the nearest whole day.',NULL,'365','One Earth year is approximately 365.25 days, which rounds to 365 days.','NASA: Earth Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/earth/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000302','ESTIMATE','About how many days does the Moon take to orbit Earth relative to distant stars? Round to one decimal place.',NULL,'27.3','The Moon’s sidereal orbital period is about 27.3 days.','NASA: Moon Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/moon/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000303','ESTIMATE','About how many degrees Celsius is the Sun’s visible surface? Round to the nearest thousand degrees.',NULL,'6000','The Sun’s photosphere is about 5,500°C, which rounds to 6,000°C at the nearest thousand.','NASA: Sun Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/sun/facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000304','ESTIMATE','About how many hours does Jupiter take to rotate once? Round to the nearest whole hour.',NULL,'10','Jupiter rotates in about 9.9 hours, which rounds to 10 hours.','NASA: Jupiter Facts','https://science.nasa.gov/jupiter/jupiter-facts/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000305','ESTIMATE','About how many kilometers long is the Grand Canyon? Round to the nearest whole kilometer.',NULL,'446','Grand Canyon National Park is about 277 miles long, approximately 446 km.','U.S. National Park Service: Grand Canyon Facts','https://www.nps.gov/grca/learn/management/statistics.htm','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000306','ESTIMATE','About how many years old is Earth, expressed in billions of years and rounded to one decimal place? Enter only the number of billions.',NULL,'4.5','Earth formed about 4.54 billion years ago, which rounds to 4.5 billion.','USGS: Age of the Earth','https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/how-old-earth','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000307','ESTIMATE','About how many kilometers is one light-year? Express your answer in trillions of kilometers and round to one decimal place.',NULL,'9.5','A light-year is about 9.46 trillion kilometers, which rounds to 9.5 trillion km.','NASA: What is a light-year?','https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanets/what-is-a-light-year/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000308','ESTIMATE','At 20°C in dry air, about how fast does sound travel in meters per second? Round to the nearest whole number.',NULL,'343','The speed of sound in air at 20°C is approximately 343 m/s.','NASA JPL: Perseverance sound recordings','https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/what-sounds-captured-by-nasas-perseverance-rover-reveal-about-mars/','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000309','ESTIMATE','How many squares are on a standard chessboard? Enter the exact count.',NULL,'64','A standard chessboard has 8 rows and 8 columns, so 8×8=64 squares.','FIDE: Laws of Chess','https://handbook.fide.com/chapter/E012023','estimate',60),
	('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000310','ESTIMATE','How many member states does the United Nations have? Enter the established count.',NULL,'193','The United Nations has 193 member states.','United Nations: Member States','https://www.un.org/en/about-us/member-states','estimate',60)
